{:edb/db-before-t 1222 :edb/db-after-t 1223 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534535 50 #inst "2026-10-07T20:58:30.950Z" 13194139534535 true] [17592186119861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293632 13194139534535 true] [17592186119861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293639 13194139534535 true] [17592186119861 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293642 13194139534535 true] [17592186119862 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293621 13194139534535 true] [17592186119862 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293628 13194139534535 true] [17592186293621 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293622 13194139534535 true] [17592186293621 1089 "q-170188" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293621 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534535 true] [17592186293621 1100 "Given a curve $x=5{y}^{5}-3{y}^{3},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-2,-1)?$" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293621 1113 #uuid "efc76f43-44f6-557f-a3e7-3700bed34dc2" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293621 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{5}-3{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{5})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (5{y}^{4})-3\\cdot (3{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =25{y}^{4}-9{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{25{y}^{4}-9{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-2,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-2,-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25(-1)^{4}-9(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-1) & =\\frac{1}{16}(x-(-2)) \\\\ y+1 & =\\frac{1}{16}(x+2) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{16}+\\frac{2}{16}-1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{16}+\\frac{1}{8}-1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{16}-\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534535 true] [1