\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293628 1113 #uuid "2042d891-4311-5637-9472-9d451beb8575" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293628 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(3y-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =3(1)-2y \\\\  & =3-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{3-2y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(0,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(0,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (x-0) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3}x+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293630 13194139534535 true] [17592186293629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293631 13194139534535 true] [17592186293629 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534535 true] [17592186293629 1041 "field-1" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293629 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293630 13194139534535 true] [17592186293629 1110 #uuid "233bc82e-fabe-5cf2-aa6d-63ee891eee94" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293630 1034 "-\\frac{x}{3}+3" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534535 true] [17592186293630 1111 #uuid "f7ea7b05-7eba-5553-b109-4cfb84fccd0e" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293631 1034 "-3x+3" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534535 true] [17592186293631 1111 #uuid "b8edf8dd-fea6-5737-be79-46ac6c949808" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293632 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293633 13194139534535 true] [17592186293632 1089 "q-32706" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293632 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534535 true] [17592186293632 1100 "If $x={y}^{5}+3y-5,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(33,2).$" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293632 1113 #uuid "96332eb9-d2e1-560a-b367-0be5b28bc2c3" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293632 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{5}+3y-5) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{5})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =5{y}^{4}+3(1)+0 \\\\  & =5{y}^{4}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{5{y}^{4}+3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(33,2),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(33,2)} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot {2}^{4}+3}=\\frac{1}{83}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293633 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293634 13194139534535 true] [17592186293633 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293635 13194139534535 true] [17592186293633 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293636 13194139534535 true] [17592186293633 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293637 13194139534535 true] [17592186293633 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293638 13194139534535 true] [17592186293633 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534535 true] [17592186293633 1041 "selection" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293633 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293634 13194139534535 true] [17592186293633 1110 #uuid "14230aa6-9a02-59c3-9fbc-02251676e493" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293634 1034 "\\frac{1}{83}" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293634 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534535 true] [17592186293634 1111 #uuid "c40962be-eb02-5bb1-90ba-9f02206d11ed" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293635 1034 "43" 13194139534535 true] [17592186293635 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534535 true] [17592186293635 1111 #uuid "c8bd0fcf-293a-5ded-9d62-